d805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T12:20:37-07:00","id":1229634,"title":"","content":"just thought on another point.<br /> <br /> A reason to tolerate members joining more then one covenant even though the bible says &quot;A servant cannot have two master's&quot;<br /> <br /> is because even if his primary loyalty lies with the other covenant and you know it, you can <br /> <br /> A: Hope to seduce him to your point of view<br /> <br /> B: It gives you a ready way to contact them<br /> <br /> e.g. if an acolyte joins the Ordo Dracul is hard working but seeks the coil of the Wyrm to be able to ride the wave more effectively and better defend her temple.<br /> <br /> The Order plays dumb because she might find she likes it there after a bit, might even renounce the circle<br /> <br /> Not Likely though.<br /> <br /> even then it hopefully lets you contact the Circle in a rush.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T12:36:44-08:00","id":1373242,"title":"","content":"Thread That was Dead Return to life!!!!!<br /> <br /> Thread Necromancer laughs Maniacly.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sorr Just Didn't want to have to create a new thread.<br /> <br /> How about A comparison on what its like to be a multi Covenant Kindred.<br /> <br /> A Sanctum Invictus Duel Member will likely be shrugged off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 03-06-2020, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T15:24:18-08:00","id":1373269,"title":"","content":"Depends on the ideologies in the specific setting. I've been in a setting where a Lancea et Sanctum and Circle of the Crone dual membership was possible. The Sanctified were moral universalists and the Crone actually took a dim view of human and kindred sacrifices save for extreme circumstances. I've played in a setting of Invictus and the Carthian Movement united to overthrow an Acolyte prince, only for them to become as virulently murderous against any religious practitioners as the Circle of the Crone was against men and non-Acolytes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T15:37:33-08:00","id":1373273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1222546-multi-covenant-membership?p=1373242#post1373242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thread That was Dead Return to life!!!!!<br /> <br /> Thread Necromancer laughs Maniacly.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sorr Just Didn't want to have to create a new thread.<br /> <br /> How about A comparison on what its like to be a multi Covenant Kindred.<br /> <br /> A Sanctum Invictus Duel Member will likely be shrugged off.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Two States for the price of one! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But then the Invictus is so pragmatic and self-serving that meshing it with anyone but the Carthians might get a similar reaction (domain''s local politics vicissitudes pending, obviously), i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T15:45:14-08:00","id":1373275,"title":"","content":"read somewhere in some book.. that In some citys the Sanctified and the Circle might unite against an extremely Secular prince from one of the other 3 Covenants too<br /> <br /> But lets Try Combinations and explore them shall we?<br /> <br /> <br /> Lancaea Sanctum/Invictus: Barely Qualifys as 'Duel Membership' at all to some Sensibletys. The Represent the 2nd Estate in the Halls of the First.<br /> <br /> Ordo Dracul/Circle of the Crone: They try to Offer their knowledge of Cruac where it Can benefit the order but not blasphemy against the Crone. And also Try to Wield Coils on behalf of the Crone (A Holy place Guarded by Someone with Coil of the Wyrm anyone? Had that idea a while but is that better accomplished with duel membership or an.... understanding between the Circle and Ordo Dracul an exchange of Favors?) <br /> <br /> <br /> any other insights?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T10:51:37-08:00","id":1373405,"title":"","content":"<b>Invictus and:</b><br /> L&amp;S: That's almost the traditional norm and perhaps more common in places where people are comfortable/apathetic with Church and State being closely linked e.g. a Westminster Creed priest (or whatever title) who doesn't challenge Invictus and basically serves a court wizard who makes social functions more ritualistic, much like holding a wedding in Church for the aesthetics.<br /> <br /> Ordo Dracul: Secret handshake &quot;old boys' club&quot; types. Keen on the Mystery of the Voivode.<br /> <br /> Circle of the Crone: This is odd, but far from implausible. Near the beginning of the <i>Circle of the Crone</i> book, it said that they had a close relationship with Invictus in Bristol, having taking the usual role of the L&amp;S. It may also be connected to established pagans who ruled before the L&amp;S arrived and persisted. And somebody posted something here about Circle of the Crone bankers or something like that in Manhattan, which might also fit Invictus.<br /> <br /> Carthian: Now this is a stretch, because the usual point of Carthians is implement a better system than Invictus offers. These could be Invictus put forward reforms and amendments without changing its definitive features or Carthians whose policies appeal to Invictus, like conservatives.<br /> <br /> <b>Lancea et Sanctum and:</b><br /> Ordo Dracul: Blasphemous, irreverent scholars. I think this would only be tolerated under exceptional circumstances (of which Requiem has plenty). Tismanu converts.<br /> <br /> Circle of the Crone: Syncretism that probably involved intentional subversion.<br /> <br /> Carthian: Spears who got sick of Invictus doing whatever they liked and taking the Second Estate for granted. Pseudo-liberation theologists. Non-conformist liberals or old school socialists. Etc.<br /> <br /> <b>Ordo Dracul and:</b><br /> Circle of the Crone: Mythic self improvement theorists. Paranormal investigators*<br /> <br /> Carthian: When someone says &quot;you can't deny our nature as vampires&quot;, this is the guy who calls bullshit. They believe that vampires can be better (whatever that means) both as individuals and societies. They may also aspire to ultimately replace the old kind of vampires.<br /> <br /> <b>Circle of the Crone and Carthian:</b> Given how pluralistic both covenants are, this could cover all sorts. Less militant members of one or the other tend to be wary because they end up getting lumped together by the First and Second estates. Think of what Pat Robertson says about feminism in <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=pat+robertson+feminism+poster&amp;client=firefox-b-d&amp;sxsrf=ALeKk00B2BpNxixGWyS2yySK9tMB9slVhw:1583604988980&amp;source=lnms&amp;tbm=isch&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwj2otSm_IjoAhVSu3EKHVGsA5sQ_AUoAXoECAwQAw&amp;biw=1525&amp;bih=730\" target=\"_blank\">that poster</a> or the concept of cultural marxism.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Now I think of it, that could also apply to a lot of worldly/mystic joint memberships, but in this case, I mean vampires who dedicate most of their time to finding what else is out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 03-07-2020, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}